        "readable_text": "Content:\nTo divide a unit fraction by a whole number, we multiply the fraction's denominator by the whole number.\n\nContent:\nFor example, to calculate [MATH: \\dfrac{1}{5} \\div {\\color{blue}2},] we multiply the fraction's denominator by [MATH: {\\color{blue}2}\\!:]\n[MATH: \\dfrac{1}{5} \\div {\\color{blue}2} = \\dfrac{1}{5 \\times {\\color{blue}2}} = \\dfrac{1}{10}]\n\nContent:\nNotice that we get the same answer using a fraction model, and the process is similar.\n\nGraphic:\n[IMG: /graphics/5ddb7251d1e11abbce9782ed282533e3]"
